{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347462-trying-to-homebrew-liminals-charm-ideas-appreciated","id":1347462,"title":"Trying to homebrew Liminals - charm ideas appreciated","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-10T06:45:54-08:00","id":1347462,"title":"Trying to homebrew Liminals - charm ideas appreciated","content":"So, I wanted to use some liminals in my campaign, but it looks like official rules won't be a thing for a bit more time, so I decided to homebrew some. <br /> <br /> While the character creation seems pretty straightforward - it could be based on dragonblooded with some tweaks the charm trees are what will likely take the most work.<br /> <br /> I'm at the early stage where I just write down charm names and what they're supposed to do. This is what I have so far.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1wz7DouDunlJP4vFYlSoDgxF6EmGmk5NX81UlyOnr-lQ/edit\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1wz7DouDunlJP4vFYlSoDgxF6EmGmk5NX81UlyOnr-lQ/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1wz7DouDunlJP4vFYlSoDgxF6EmGmk5NX81UlyOnr-lQ/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1wz7DouDunlJP4vFYlSoDgxF6EmGmk5NX81UlyOnr-lQ/edit </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Rather than making a charm tree for each skill like with other exalts, I decided to go for themed trees, three for each aspect - there are some skills where being a liminal doesn't seem to apply at all.<br /> <br /> I've scavenged oWoD for some ideas, and added some of my own, but I still need a lot more, at least 15 charms per tree.<br /> <br /> Do you have any ideas you think could be added there?<br /> Or perhaps some of mine look like they could use some work because of possible balance isues or not quite fitting the theme? (from what I understand, the liminals themes are &quot;messing with their own bodies&quot;, &quot;messing with strong emotions&quot; and &quot;messing with the line between life and death, but no actual necromancy&quot; Did I get it right?) <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T07:06:25-08:00","id":1347466,"title":"","content":"Find and read <i>Embalming: The Another Tale of Frankenstein</i>.<br /> <br /> It's made by the same man who made <i>Rurouni Kenshin</i> and <i>Buso Renkin</i>. The gimmick of that universe is making Frankenstein monsters with freaky new biological features, many of them taken to a supernatural extreme.<br /> <br /> You've got characters who harden their skin into armor, characters that treat their flesh like rubber, characters that dangerously accelerate their heart-rate for super-strength or to pressurize cutting blasts of their own blood, and characters that leave extra eyeballs all over the place as security cameras.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T07:11:04-08:00","id":1347468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347462-trying-to-homebrew-liminals-charm-ideas-appreciated?p=1347466#post1347466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Find and read <i>Embalming: The Another Tale of Frankenstein</i>.<br /> <br /> It's made by the same man who made <i>Rurouni Kenshin</i> and <i>Buso Renkin</i>. The gimmick of that universe is making Frankenstein monsters with freaky new biological features, many of them taken to a supernatural extreme.<br /> <br /> You've got characters who harden their skin into armor, characters that treat their flesh like rubber, characters that dangerously accelerate their heart-rate for super-strength or to pressurize cutting blasts of their own blood, and characters that leave extra eyeballs all over the place as security cameras.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My list already has 3 out of 4 of those.<br /> <br /> Have you read Franken Fran?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T07:39:10-08:00","id":1347470,"title":"","content":"The manga *Claymore* has been cited as potential inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T07:42:05-08:00","id":1347471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347462-trying-to-homebrew-liminals-charm-ideas-appreciated?p=1347468#post1347468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> My list already has 3 out of 4 of those.<br /> <br /> Have you read Franken Fran?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, and never.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T08:51:17-08:00","id":1347479,"title":"","content":"Have you read the Liminals preview from the 3rd ed Kickstarter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T09:55:37-08:00","id":1347490,"title":"","content":"Just use Dragon-Blooded charms and change the fluff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T12:27:48-08:00","id":1347535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347462-trying-to-homebrew-liminals-charm-ideas-appreciated?p=1347479#post1347479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you read the Liminals preview from the 3rd ed Kickstarter?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think so. I asked about liminals before, and got linked to a page worth of text about how they come into existence and how they fit into Creation.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T18:06:21-08:00","id":1347583,"title":"","content":"Working through dragonblooded charms that could be reworked. <br /> <br /> In the meantime, one thing I have no idea what to do with is anima powers. What do you think they should do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T07:38:19-08:00","id":1347677,"title":"","content":"Flesh Aspects should have something useful for combat that helps them fulfill the fantasy of being Alex Mercer from the [Prototype] game. Maybe they're just stronger or tougher, or maybe they can better avoid ruining body-parts for Charms that carry sacrificial costs, or maybe they have the easiest time replacing ruined parts with new parts (especially parts taken from the refuse of the battlefield).<br /> <br /> They're the Aspect meant to represent the Frankenstein's Monster who is unstoppably violent. The uncontrollable and relentless abomination that destroys everything in its path. That is, after all, what their creators intended them to be even before the Dark Mother breathed life into them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T14:31:46-08:00","id":1347765,"title":"","content":"The three charm trees I have for Flesh are<br /> Instinct (since they're born of violent intent) - giving their bodies hysterical strength, but also manipulating anger in others, and boosting their reactions.<br /> Transformation (stretching, contorting, doing some on the spot modifications to adjust to the situation<br /> Absorbtion (fixing themselves with transplants, getting abilities through transplants, and being able to do it supernaturally fast.<br /> <br /> Adding excellencies to charm trees now - the distribution isn't symmetrical at all, with Breath covering a lot of abilities.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T16:45:00-08:00","id":1347792,"title":"","content":"I personally look at the body warping Lunars can do, with the important distinction that Liminals have to pay lipservice to conservation of mass and are supposed to replace their bodyparts overtime.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T16:15:23-08:00","id":1348041,"title":"","content":"Since stitched flesh juggernaut doesn't require a a corpse to start it, just to reset it, it could be the other way round - the conservation of mass doesn't apply much, and at high essence they can go full Attack on Titan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T04:31:52-08:00","id":1348215,"title":"","content":"It doesn't apply much because that'd turn their powers into a simulationist bookkeeping nightmare, but that's still more than Lunars which is &quot;not at all, watch as I turn from a mouse into a yeddim!&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T06:42:00-08:00","id":1348249,"title":"","content":"And now I have a vision of a fat, hairy lunar sitting on an abyssal.<br /> <br /> I'm 3/4 done digging through dragonblooded charms for inspiration. I can already see there will be some issues with my version (some charm trees being much bigger than others, or charms of the same skill split all over the place) - but better imperfect than nonexistent.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, coming back to a previous question - what do you think liminal anima banners should do beyond making them look creepy?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T17:06:17-08:00","id":1348578,"title":"","content":"Ok, the first attempt at flesh, since that's what most people seem the most excited about.<br /> This is one of the three skill trees focusing on flesh aspect (the other two geared towards absorbing body parts, and manipulating agression respectively)<br /> <br /> Do you think it contains all it should? Are the charms on proper Essence levels or should something be moved around? Do you have idea for anything else that should be added?<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">__________________________________________________ ______________________________________</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Path of transformation</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (powers transforming the liminal\u2019s own body)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Essence 1</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* flesh meets the demand - athletics excellency: the body subtly reshapes to aid in the action attempted.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* fine-tuned senses - awareness excellency: manipulates sense organs for best effects.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* sculpted visage - transforms the exalt\u2019s appearance - helps in disguise attempts, and at the least hides his true identity.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* shifting eyes of a predator - see in the dark</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* nose of a hunter - detect enemies by smell.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* swallow the scroll case - hides a small item by embedding it in the exalt\u2019s flesh.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* reject the constraints of flesh - freely disconnect joints, to escape a limb lock, or slip out of manacles. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* rigid flesh barrier - parry a weapon attack with brawl, reduce damage from a withering attack.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Essence 2</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* shifting flesh redistribution - temporarily move (essence) dots between physical attributes.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* slingshot of tendon - stretch the exalt\u2019s limbs to launch him a considerable distance.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* stitched flesh juggernaut - (in core book) gain temporary muscle mass for a scene.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* clambering horror chase - (in core book) deform limbs to supplement a rush action or climb walls.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* gruesome bow - string a bow with the exalt\u2019s own tendon, increasing damage for a scene (can be combined with ivory wasp stinger from path of bone to create a temporary artifact bow) </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* whip of flesh - strike out one range band away by dislocating joints and stretching tendons.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* constricting coils - wraps around opponent, supplementing grapple control roll.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* five fingered spider dance - detach a body part and control it remotely.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Essence 3</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* vise of sucking flesh - counter a decisive attack with a disarm attempt, trapping the blade in bulging muscles. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* coiled flesh technique - squeeze through any space the skull can fit through.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* movements of the gruesome puzzle - control all body parts even while decapitated.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* puppet pulls her own strings - keep damaged body parts together with essence, to reduce wound penalties, or temporarily negate crippling injury.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* bludgeon of flesh - grow a limb out of size, giving the brawl attack characteristics of an artifact weapon of chosen size.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* shapeshifting arsenal - bludgeon of flesh can gain a different weapon attribute (such as smashing) each turn.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* wed to pain - commit essence motes to negate wound penalties.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* watchful eye - remove the exalt\u2019s eye from its socket to observe an area, learning of what it has seen once it is retrieved.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Essence 4</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* string of corpses - stretch and deform limbs to grapple multiple opponents.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* eye of the sentry - improvement over watchful eye, allows remote observation.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* monstrous growth - briefly grow 15 feet tall - the exalt is left emaciated and weak after the effect ends.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Essence 5</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* devouring rage - turn into a shapeshifting monster, gaining improved movement speed, strength, durability and a free withering attack each turn from grasping tendrils. The body starts burning out fairly quickly, and leaves the exalt skeletal and bloodied when over, but decisive attacks, or withering attacks against battle groups, allow him to absorb flesh to heal and keep the effect going through an extended battle. </span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T16:56:06-08:00","id":1348752,"title":"","content":"Just as a note, Liminals have been stated to be Attribute-based Exalted, like Lunars are, instead of Ability-based Exalted like DBs or Solars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T18:52:41-08:00","id":1348767,"title":"","content":"As mentioned in the opening post, this version is neither.<br /> <br /> It just occured to me - since some of the powers would be awkward to use with equipment like armor... would it cause any balance issues if a liminal could graft sockets into his body?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T19:04:17-08:00","id":1348769,"title":"","content":"Yet they... have Ability Excellencies? Alright then","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T19:23:34-08:00","id":1348772,"title":"","content":"Well, the excellencies need to be connected to either an ability or an attribute. <br /> With themes attatched to aspects it was easier to fluff them that way ( how would you describe a liminal wits excellency for example?)<br /> <br /> That being said, if you make a compelling argument to start over from scratch your way, this is the last moment to do so - i know from experience that major rewrites are death to big projects.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T19:58:41-08:00","id":1348777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347462-trying-to-homebrew-liminals-charm-ideas-appreciated?p=1348772#post1348772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the excellencies need to be connected to either an ability or an attribute.<br /> With themes attatched to aspects it was easier to fluff them that way ( how would you describe a liminal wits excellency for example?)<br /> <br /> That being said, if you make a compelling argument to start over from scratch your way, this is the last moment to do so - i know from experience that major rewrites are death to big projects.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how it would be stranger than describing a Lunar Wits Excellency?<br /> <br /> For a Liminal I guess you'd say broken down parts of their brain light up, connecting the dots in front of them. Or they tap the war memories of one of the people they took limbs from in order to roll a better join battle.<br /> <br /> <br /> But more importantly, your Athletics and Awareness Excellencies are <b>actually </b>described as attribute based effects, <b>not</b> as ability based effects. Reshaping the body to adapt to the task at hand is a physical Attribute Excellency, not a an ability Excellency (it's literally what Lunars do). Similarly, manipulating sense organs is very much a Perception Excellency, not an Awareness one.<br /> <br /> If you want to go with Ability based Excellencies, it's your call, but then the description of those Excellencies should be effects based on the Liminal's skills, not how they shape and use their body (which highlights why Ability Excellencies are weird on a Liminal in the first place).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T20:00:27-08:00","id":1348778,"title":"","content":"A Liminal Wits Excellency sounds like them channeling the fluid rush of blood or the refreshing insight of breath into their reflexes and reactions to make them lightning fast or awfully thorough. Strength channels the might of the flesh, Dexterity the fluidity of blood, Stamina the endurance of the soil, or however else you want to set them up.<br /> <br /> Excellencies are the most basic powers of the Chosen, so they don't exactly need to be super flavorful besides making the barest amount of sense. The less basic and more advanced their Charms become, the more they need to be tied to the Liminal archetypes or Aspects instead of the Attributes in general. For example, Strength starts with basic &quot;Gain extra Strength for feats of strength etc&quot; with basic adherence to Liminal themes but nothing you wouldn't see in other splats most of the time with some refluffing, and then as you progress becomes more and more about turning limbs into monstrous oversized battering rams or crushing bones with a fleshrot-carrying bite and so on. <br /> <br /> Considering I'm working on a Liminal brew myself and have about fifty Charms in the works, the approach seems to be working just fine, if you treat them like DBs in power level but slightly higher at greater/more gruesome costs, great ease to take and recover from crippling injuries, limited immortality, and Attribute Charms instead of Ability ones. And of course, having their own themes to draw from, which makes them feel a lot different than DBs while retaining similar levels of supernatural competence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T05:01:01-08:00","id":1348830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347462-trying-to-homebrew-liminals-charm-ideas-appreciated?p=1348772#post1348772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With themes attatched to aspects it was easier to fluff them that way ( how would you describe a liminal wits excellency for example?)</div> </div> </div> </div> You don't actually <i>need</i> to fluff Excellencies. they're baselines prowess, representing the general quality of being superhuman that all Exalted share.<br /> <br /> Considering your current structure, though, I think it might be easier to have one Excellency per path, in the manner of 2e's Infernal Excellencies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T07:13:31-08:00","id":1348854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347462-trying-to-homebrew-liminals-charm-ideas-appreciated?p=1348830#post1348830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You don't actually <i>need</i> to fluff Excellencies. they're baselines prowess, representing the general quality of being superhuman that all Exalted share.<br /> <br /> Considering your current structure, though, I think it might be easier to have one Excellency per path, in the manner of 2e's Infernal Excellencies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have enough paths to cover all abilities. I tried coming up with more, but then didn't have enough distinct charm ideas - 3 per aspect seems the most that is workable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T13:53:17-08:00","id":1348924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347462-trying-to-homebrew-liminals-charm-ideas-appreciated?p=1348777#post1348777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But more importantly, your Athletics and Awareness Excellencies are <b>actually </b>described as attribute based effects, <b>not</b> as ability based effects. Reshaping the body to adapt to the task at hand is a physical Attribute Excellency, not a an ability Excellency (it's literally what Lunars do). Similarly, manipulating sense organs is very much a Perception Excellency, not an Awareness one.</div> </div> </div> </div>If my joints shift position to give me better leverage, it doesn't affect my strength - just my ability to apply it. <br /> Part of the problem might be that the two excellencies I posted are tied to the path of transformation, tying them strongly to flesh aspect - that's how flesh generally does things, and skills under other aspects work differently (for example, lore is tied to soil, by remembering bits of things that were forgotten, while investigation works with marrow, by making the liminal obsessively inquisitive. <b>Perhaps the solution is moving them to different paths to change the descriptions?</b><br /> <br /> <b>So far, the distribution looks as follows:</b><br /> <br /> <b>FLESH</b><br /> <b>Transformation:</b> changing the liminal's body in various ways, from stretching and deforming to temporary increases in size. The excellencies are <b>athletics</b> and <b>awareness</b>.<br /> <b>Instinct:</b> flesh liminals are born of agression, and some of their powers reflect that. Instinct covers overclocking the liminal's body, enhancing performance by primal instincts, and also manipulating the agression of others, much like the Gangrel in VtM could. The excellencies are <b>brawl</b> and <b>thrown</b> <br /> <b>Absorbtion:</b> the ability to fix liminals body by taking flesh from corpses. It starts with basic ability to fix himself, then makes it faster, allows taking abilities from transplants, and even use it on other people to a limited extent. The instinctive understanding of the ways of the flesh provides <b>medicine</b> excellency.<br /> <br /> <b>BLOOD</b><br /> <b>Passion:</b> blood liminals are born of greed and lust. they can gain instinctive understanding on these emotions, reading and manipulating them. The path of passion provides about one third of a liminal's social charms, including <b>socialise</b>, <b>performance</b> and <b>linguistics</b> excellencies.<br /> <b>Blood:</b> this path is a mixed bag of blood magic - from being able to smell it over long distances, to sealing pacts in blood, attracting ghosts, or messing with another person's blood pressure. It has no assigned excellencies.<br /> <b>Viscera:</b> direct applications of blood magic, largely inspired by blood shintai from VtM Kindred of the East: controlling blood to form grabbing tendrils, a magical whip, or a blinding cloud of red mist. It has no assigned excellencies.<br /> <br /> <b>MARROW</b><br /> <b>Obsession:</b> obsession is the source of marrow liminals, and this path lets them harness it's power - whether to distract the guards, make themselves a center of attention, or work like a man possessed when a big task is to be completed. It provides excellencies for <b>investigation</b> and <b>craft</b>.<br /> <b>Essence: </b>the source of a body's resilience rests withing its bones. The path of essence allows the liminal to manipulate his internal energy, whether to make him harder to kill, store essence away for later use, or brew dangerous poisons inside his body. It is responsible for <b>resistance</b> excellency.<br /> <b>Bone:</b> through the essence flowing through his marrow, a liminal's skeleton can be dramatically reshaped. This path shapes his bones into tools, weapons, and sometimes even armor, and lets him better attune to things being an extension of his body - it provides <b>melee</b> and <b>archery</b> excellencies.<br /> <br /> <b>BREATH</b><br /> <b>Despair:</b> the breath liminals are born of despair. Mastering its power lets them sap the will of their enemies, dull intimacies, intimidate foes, or fool emotion reading by feigning numb indifference. The gravitas that comes with their frightening aura provides for the <b>presence</b> excellency.<br /> <b>Breath:</b> the nature of breath is to match the body it passes through. The air is untouchable, yet everpresent. The powers of breath let the liminal manipulate air much like an air dragonborn would - but also fit in, meet the expectations of others, and get out of their way both figuratively and literally. The versatile path provides excellencies for<b> sail, bureaucracy, stealth, dodge</b> and <b>larceny.</b><br /> <b>Life:</b> breath is life, and it is the nature of life to spread. By sharing the gift of life with his surroundings, the liminal can expect help from every tool he uses, and even awaken objects to motion (including dead bodies, though they become flesh puppets rather than undead - the Dark Mother would not approve of necromancy). Attuning to the forces of life provides <b>survival</b> and <b>ride</b> excellencies.<br /> <br /> <b>SOIL:</b><br /> <b>Grave:</b> the liminals are tools of death, and their path is always connected to the grave. The pull of death lets the liminal rot his enemies and decompose objects, but also manipulate grave goods, sleep safely underground, or &quot;bury&quot; a weapon, retrieving it from the earth when needed. <br /> <b>Memory: </b>they say a man is truly dead only when he is forgotten. Bound to the forces of death, the liminal can tap into memories to experience flashbacks, learn and understand things, or manipulate them to make others forget of his existence or deeds. The powers of memory provide excellencies for<b> lore, war</b> and <b>integrity</b>. <br /> <b>Threshold:</b> stuck between life and death a liminal walks two worlds. This gives him powers to interact with spirtis, enter the underworld, or even move through solid objects like a ghost. the path provides the <b>occult</b> excellency as well as access to <b>sorcery</b>. <br /> <br /> So, if you were to shuffle it around, how would you do it? <br /> And if I were to change excellencies to reflect attributes, which paths should I put them in? or perhaps they should belong to no path at all?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T14:20:46-08:00","id":1348926,"title":"","content":"The way I have it, Strength and Appearance reflect Flesh, Dexterity and Perception reflect Blood, Manipulation and Stamina reflect Soil, Wits and Charisma reflect Breath, and Intelligence reflects Marrow. Since there's no real way to make them proportionate, trick's just not worrying too much about it and going with what feels about right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T15:45:38-08:00","id":1348955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347462-trying-to-homebrew-liminals-charm-ideas-appreciated?p=1348854#post1348854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have enough paths to cover all abilities. I tried coming up with more, but then didn't have enough distinct charm ideas - 3 per aspect seems the most that is workable.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm not proposing that you make one path for each Ability, but rather that each path should gets its own broadly-applicable Excellency.<br /> <br /> For example, the Path of Instinct would have an Excellency that can enhance actions relying on intuition, madness, gut feeling, recklessness, and (of course) instinct, but which can't be used when you require patience, long-term thinking, or strategy.<br /> <br /> (I have some actual Charm ideas for you too, but I need to gather my thoughts and actually write them down.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347462-trying-to-homebrew-liminals-charm-ideas-appreciated?p=1348926#post1348926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I have it, Strength and Appearance reflect Flesh, Dexterity and Perception reflect Blood, Manipulation and Stamina reflect Soil, Wits and Charisma reflect Breath, and Intelligence reflects Marrow. Since there's no real way to make them proportionate, trick's just not worrying too much about it and going with what feels about right.</div> </div> </div> </div> My personal setup leaves <b>Blood</b> with Charisma (passion, connections) and Wits (purity, but also navigation and guidance), <b>Breath</b> with Dexterity (grace and subtle action) and Perception (understanding and reflection),<b> Flesh</b> with your set of Strength (force, madness, savagery) and Appearance (metamorphosis and lust), <b>Marrow</b> with Manipulation (secrecy) and Intelligence (analysis, obsession), and <b>Soil</b> with Stamina (resilience, resurrection) and Intelligence (mysticism, creation).<br /> <br /> Given that <i>Masters of Jade</i> introduced Liminals as &quot;sorcerer-exorcists&quot;, among other things, it seems appropriate that Intelligence would be the only Attribute to appear twice (Stamina, I suppose, would be the other option). Like Lunars, I can also see a set of Universal Charms dedicated to the central promise of <i>Frankenstein's monster</i> and <i>ghost hunter </i>\u2013 hardiness and anti-spirit Charms, with more specific effects branching off into the Attribute trees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 11-16-2019, 07:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T17:33:45-08:00","id":1349470,"title":"","content":"I think the way I described it, it would be:<br /> Strength and Appearance for Flesh<br /> Charisma and Dexterity for Blood<br /> Manipulation and Wits for Breath<br /> Stamina and Perception for Marrow<br /> and Intelligence for Soil.<br /> <br /> Sorry for not posting anything more - busy monday.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T00:15:40-08:00","id":1349794,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Path of instinct</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (powers dealing with aggression and primal instincts)</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Essence 1</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* pulse of the living herd - can run through crowds without being slowed or trampled (the one exception is a battle group purposefully trying to pin him down)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* primal response - supplements block or dodge by boosting natural reflexes.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* chase the true target - supplements a disengage towards a different enemy.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Essence 2</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* braving the raging rapids - supplement a dodge by misdirecting the attacker\u2019s killing intent.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* frenzied strength - gains a boost of strength at the cost of bashing damage at the end of the scene.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* blow of blind fury - boost damage of an attack, at the cost of damage that becomes apparent at the end of the scene, possibly ruining the arm if used consecutively.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* fool stumbles in anger - counter a social attack by causing the target to get emotional and forget himself - if it peels off all of the opponent\u2019s successes, it can cause a botch and embarrass him.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* smell the killing intent - supplements awareness roll (opposite stealth, or join battle) when enemy initiates hostilities, depending on the attacker\u2019s intimacies.<br /> * frightening savagery - push the enemy back with savage attacks, increasing the overwhelming value of your weapon.<br /> * furious onslaught - prevent the target from recovering from onslaught penalty on his next turn.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Essence 3</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* curse of blind rage - after a successful dodge, redirect the attack to a different target within range</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* balancing of the humors - calm down or enrage a target.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* anger unquenched - resist social or psyche influence (such as fear effects) that try to end the fight.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* savage anger defense - fly into a rage in response to a psyche effect.<br /> * eager predator's method - </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">pay motes to gain (essence) extra initiative from crashing an opponent.<br /> * thrashing beast's grip - get (essence) motes refund on motes paid during a savage in grapple.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Essence 4</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* tooth and claw kata - reflexively clash a close combat attack with a withering attack - if victorious, can immediately initiate a gambit, even if already acted.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* frantic heartbeat of the beast - enrage a battle group<br /> * savage hunter's strike - gain extra attack dice against a crashed opponent.<br /> * Sating the burning anger - upon taking down a non-trivial opponent, pay motes to recover a point of willpower.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Essence 5</b><br /> * killer's momentum - retain (wits) extra initiative after incapacitating an enemy with a decisive attack.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Not the shortest path I have so far (that would be life) but it could definitely use some additional ideas. </b></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23788,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","user":"Braininthejar","date":". 11-21-2019, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T10:38:23-08:00","id":1349887,"title":"","content":"I always got a Liminal feel from iZombie. You could make a whole tree out of what Liv does eating brains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4915-darkuwa","name":"Darkuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4915_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T15:10:19-08:00","id":1349929,"title":"","content":"Well, the the third path for Flesh is Absorbtion, allowing the liminals to gain powers by replacing body parts - but the brain is one thing that is by rules tot replacable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T05:49:35-08:00","id":1350004,"title":"","content":"Nobody has any ideas to add for the path of instinct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T07:43:03-08:00","id":1350013,"title":"","content":"Instinct should imo feel swingy but very rewarding if the swing goes your way. Stuff that causes 1s on an opponent's roll to subtract successes, advantages that you roll for (Such as rolling the initiative you gain after crashing an opponent and healing non-aggravated health levels equal to the successes while losing that much initiative), and conditional powers that pay off really well if the conditions are met. I don't have exact ideas since I find it hard to work with an Essence-based approach, but capturing the feel of the tree and the Liminal themes and archetypes should help come up with ideas for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T09:11:11-08:00","id":1350023,"title":"","content":"Come to think of iit, some charm ideas can be split - with several effects of similar description but different mechanical benefits.<br /> <br /> EDIT: it did give me some ideas, and I got 4 extra charms out of it. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23788,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","user":"Braininthejar","date":". 11-21-2019, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T13:26:25-08:00","id":1350100,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Ok then. The last path for Flesh is the path of Absorbtion. 19 charms so far, could use a few more.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Path of Absorption</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (powers dealing with absorbing body parts and features from other creatures.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Essence 1</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* body graft - basic ability to repair the liminal\u2019s body with other people\u2019s body parts. Takes a minimum of medical skill, but is rather time-consuming.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* carrion birds waiting - quicken medical diagnosis to a miscellaneous action. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* graft the warrior\u2019s arm - gain ranks in a physical skill (melee, brawl, dodge, archery, thrown, athletics, etc) until the end of adventure, by grafting a body part from a skilled person.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Essence 2</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* graft the dancer\u2019s feet - gain ranks in fine motor or specialised skill ( larceny, craft, perform, sail, survival, etc) until the end of adventure, by grafting a body part from a skilled person.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* snake sheds skin - absorb the face of a dead body to create a disguise.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* patchwork body reconstruction - (in book) heals himself on a killing blow.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* wisdom of carrion - skills obtained by graft powers can be persisted by investing essence.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* commanding the ways of the flesh - improve medicine effect on another creature.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* tendon-weaving spider - when taking another\u2019s body parts, reduce the operation to one scene. At extra mote cost, remove the need for surgical tools.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Essence 3</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* graft the sage\u2019s tongue - gain intellectual or social skill ( socialise, bureaucracy, lore, occult, investigation, etc) until the end of adventure, by grafting a body part from a skilled person.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* the sum of humanity - skills persisted with wisdom of carrion can be bought permanently at XP discount. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* fluid flesh prana - improves on tendon-weaving spider; the procedure now takes an action.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* twin hearts beating - melds into another person, sharing injuries to keep both alive. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* flowing flesh patching - trade health levels for healing an ally.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* colossus of flesh - absorbs nearby dead bodies, forming a grotesque giant around the liminal - it rots away at the end of the scene unless extended with will points.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Essence 4</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* cauldron of human flesh - absorb pieces of limbs and organs into a fleshy hump as a reserve for instant repairs, gaining temporary extra health levels that can pay for self-damaging charms, or instantly heal crippling injuries accepted to mitigate damage.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* nightmarish chirurgeon - can apply flesh grafts to other people - they don\u2019t get any abilities, but can be quickly healed from life-threatening or debilitating injuries. Non-exalts will be disfigured to various extent.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Essence 5</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* bargain of the grave - nightmarish chirurgeon can commit a mote to the graft, allowing it to be destroyed at will, leaving the patient a hostage to the exalt. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* Dark Mother\u2019s mandate - improves colossus of flesh, allowing it to drag in corpses from a larger area and grow to legendary size. With sufficient bodies, it gains multiple health tracks, and needs to be whittled down like a battle group.<br /> <br /> <b>Do you have any ideas to add here?<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm actually a bit concerned with the abiity absorbtion powers. Most exalted characters are spoiled for ability dots, so these won't be useful for that long, and the XP discount for <i>the sum of humanity</i> would have to be massive to even have this part of the charm tree pay for itself. </b></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23788,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","user":"Braininthejar","date":". 11-22-2019, 07:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T15:19:38-08:00","id":1350526,"title":"","content":"A smattering of ideas, a few of them derived directly from your Path outlines.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><ul><li><b>Centipede Skin Curse: </b>While disguised, the Liminal can curse someone to take on her own appearance. If she's disguised with Snake Sheds Skin, she can transfer that Charm instead.</li> <li><b>Honey of Iron:</b> Wreathing herself in the alluring promise of blood, the Liminal penalizes non-reflexive actions and Perception rolls unless they target her. This Charm only affects the undead, unless the Liminal has Horror Haze active.</li> <li><b>Black Teeth Smile:</b> The Liminal can instill positive or sexual Intimacies towards herself in undead targets, and key persuade actions off such Intimacies, even if this would normally constitute unacceptable influence.</li> <li><b>The Pallid Promise: </b>Something in the Liminal's graveborn nature calls to the living, allowing her to treat Intimacies of disgust or fear as ones of fascination or attraction instead.</li> <li><b>The Heart and the Mind: </b>The Liminal's heart swells in her chest, blossoming into a secondary brain at the center of her being. This sharpens her mental faculties, but also allows her to recover from beheadings and brain damage that would normally be permanently fatal.</li> <li><b>Seal of the Eye and the Tongue: </b>By disabling one or more of her senses, the Liminal enhances the ones she has left. Each sense lost bestows a unique benefit, and disabling a missing sense (such as sight for a Liminal who has recently lost her eyes) is free.</li> <li><b>Living Coffin Oracle:</b> This charm requires the Liminal to surrender all of her senses with Seal of the Eye and the Tongue, awakening an otherworldly intuition in their stead. She gains all the benefits of the prerequisite with none of the drawbacks, as she simply <i>knows</i> what she cannot perceive.</li> <li><b>Groaning in the Earth: </b>The Liminal can sense her creator and the subject of any of her Defining Intimacies from afar, and she can allow them to sense her in turn. This Charm activates automatically and for free when a character is in danger, as long as the Liminal could come to their aid in time.</li> <li><b>Sacred Flesh:</b> Implanting or feeding a part of herself to a mortal, the Liminal endows them with a minor supernatural power. Anyone benefitting from Sacred Flesh is a valid target for Groaning in the Earth.</li> <li><b>Way of All Flesh:</b> The Liminal disappears into her anima and emerges from the body of a beneficiary of Sacred Flesh. This does no harm to the subject, but consumes the implant and ends the benefits of Sacred Flesh.</li> <li><b>Voice-Drinking Solitude: </b>With a subtle inhalation, the Liminal drains spoken social influence of its efficacy. Once per scene, successfully negating an influence attempt allows her to reflexively target the speaker with Steal the Gift of Life.</li> <li><b>No Voice to Cry Suffering: </b>Screaming until her voice dies, the Liminal affirms her own existence to negate a Psyche effect or baleful enchantment affecting her. This is a mystical sacrifice as much as a physical one, preventing her from regaining her voice by any means until the end of the current story. She can gain Liminal Experience from her muteness as if it was a Flaw.</li> <li><b>Hundred Heartbeats Curse:</b> Condemning the deathless to live, the Liminal makes them as fragile as the mortals beneath their feet. This strips a target of the Exalted Healing Merit and negates any passive immunity to poison or disease, even if it derives from a lack of the requisite biology. Active immunities, such as the Charms of the Exalted, suffer a Willpower surcharge instead.</li> <li><b>Embodied Earth Prison Seal:</b> The Liminal seals a defeated spirit in one of her limbs or organs, accepting a crippling injury to deny her victim rebirth. She can safely remove and replace the sacrificed flesh without releasing the spirit, but if it is destroyed, the spirit breaks free. Additionally, the Liminal can meditate to commune with the spirits she carries with her, treating them as tutors for sorcery, martial arts, and other subjects appropriate to the spirits in question.</li> </ul><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T21:29:00-08:00","id":1350578,"title":"","content":"How is Black Teeth Smile supposed to work? I'm pretty sure you can seduce ghosts in Exalted...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T06:46:29-08:00","id":1350637,"title":"","content":"It can target any kind of undead, physical or incorporeal, and allows you to influence mindless zombies and nihilistic entities like nephwracks, which would usually be impervious to positive influence.<br /> <br /> As a side effect, you can also seduce a ghost regardless of their sexuality, but I mostly wrote the Charm so that a Liminal could turn a necromancer's undead minions against them or negotiate passage from monstrous gatekeepers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T11:33:25-08:00","id":1350679,"title":"","content":"Oh...<br /> <br /> The mental image of trying to seduce a spine chain is not something my day needed...<br /> <br /> Great idea though.<br /> <br /> <br /> Way of all flesh - the name sounds more like a decay effect. Won't it leave the recipent with a gaping hole in their bodies?<br /> <br /> The heart and the mind - the only one I don't like - it circumvents a liminal's specific weakness defining to his kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23788,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","user":"Braininthejar","date":". 11-24-2019, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T16:52:16-08:00","id":1350732,"title":"","content":"Well, Lunars have a weakness in their Tell, and they get ways to hide it better through Charms. And this wouldn't circumvent that weakness, simply make it doubly hard to kill a Liminal without drowning them. I could see it, fits their body horror themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T13:35:01-08:00","id":1350898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347462-trying-to-homebrew-liminals-charm-ideas-appreciated?p=1350679#post1350679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh...<br /> <br /> The mental image of trying to seduce a spine chain is not something my day needed...<br /> <br /> Great idea though.</div> </div> </div> </div> Keep in mind that the Charm can instill and exploit any kind of positive Intimacy, not just sexual ones. I called out the latter to add a touch of the grotesque to an otherwise very basic Charm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Way of all flesh - the name sounds more like a decay effect. Won't it leave the recipent with a gaping hole in their bodies? </div> </div> </div> Picture the implanted Sacred Flesh seeping harmlessly out of the target before unfurling into the Liminal, or the target temporarily becoming a cancerous portal for the Exalted; it's not supposed to hurt them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The heart and the mind - the only one I don't like - it circumvents a liminal's specific weakness defining to his kind. </div> </div> </div> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23684_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23684\" data-vbnamecard=\"23684\">Alistair</a> gets it, though if you don't like it, you don't like it.<br /> <br /> Consider the possibility of the secondary brain being less intelligent than a Liminal's initial one, though, leaving her more animalistic or single-minded until she can reattach her head or replace her brain (which would probably come with side effects no matter how the heart-brain functions).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T07:30:38-08:00","id":1351475,"title":"","content":"Is there any template for making charm trees, or would I have to draw one in Paint?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T08:31:55-08:00","id":1351482,"title":"","content":"There are some programs that make it... easier-ish? Inkscape, say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T09:31:58-08:00","id":1351494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347462-trying-to-homebrew-liminals-charm-ideas-appreciated?p=1351475#post1351475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any template for making charm trees, or would I have to draw one in Paint?</div> </div> </div> </div>draw.io lets you draw basic charm trees fairly easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T10:22:14-08:00","id":1351504,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Path of passion</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(powers manipulating emotions of the living and the dead)</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Essence 1</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* tasting the greed - helps to find the target\u2019s price for a barter attempt.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* rose-cheeked courtesan countenance - supplements a seduction attempt.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* discern the doomed heart - detect lustful or possessive intimacies in targets.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Essence 2</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* blood money - creates an illusion of opulence, by making everything the exalt wears seem more attractive.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* lure of the bloody cup - nearby ghosts and undead are attracted to your location.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* sweet lie self inflicted - pulls upon the target\u2019s intimacy to make him want to believe you, making a lie more plausible.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* possessive strength - imbues another person with extra dice to use when acting on lust, jealousy or greed.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* blood calligraphy - by mixing her blood with the ink, the exalt can apply her appearance to a written social attack, as if she were physically present.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">the pallid promise: </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Something in the Liminal's graveborn nature calls to the living, allowing her to treat Intimacies of disgust or fear as ones of fascination or attraction instead.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">black teeth smile:</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Liminal can instill positive or sexual Intimacies towards herself in undead targets, and key persuade actions off such Intimacies, even if this would normally constitute unacceptable influence.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">honey of iron:</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Wreathing herself in the alluring promise of blood, the Liminal penalizes non-reflexive actions and Perception rolls unless they target her. This Charm only affects the undead, unless the Liminal has Horror Haze active.</span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Essence 3</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* red preached tempts to sin - sweet lie self-inflicted can now affect groups.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* love\u2019s scarlet nightmare - the next time the target acts on a targeted intimacy, it will be inverted to negative (such as turning love into jealous rage)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* forbidden fruit - tempts target to crime, causing an intimacy to overcome their inhibitions.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* words set fire to blood - temporarily strengthen a possessive intimacy, which can incite violence.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* passion eater - regain a point of will with a successful seduction attempt.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* essence of life - fill a small blood sacrifice with raw emotion, allowing a ghost to regain a point of will. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* dance of the carnal lure - fascinate a group of targets for a scene.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Essence 4</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* heart-gripping poetry - inspire strong emotions through letter.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* a poem written in blood - upgrade of blood calligraphy, allows the use of appearance-related charms.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Essence 5</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* third act blood splattered tragedy - words set fire to blood, possessive strength, forbidden fruit, and love\u2019s scarlet nightmare can now be used on groups.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T10:29:56-08:00","id":1351508,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Path of blood</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(various kinds of blood magic)</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Essence 1</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* weeping crimson gaze - (in book) see ghosts and targets for critical strikes.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* bloodthirsty arrow - enchant projectile to home on the vitals of living targets.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* predator\u2019s flicking tongue - smells blood on injured or just splattered creatures. supplements awareness and survival (tracking) rolls.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Essence 2</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* treacherous heartbeat - pinpoint locations of living creatures nearby</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* bleeding spite technique - smear your blood on the blade, making it burn the living and supernatural alike.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* curse of the bloodied bait - splash the target with your blood, cursing it to smell tasty to supernatural horrors.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* flash of the hideous - instantly flips appearance to negative to supplement intimidation attempt.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Essence 3</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* truth in the blood - pose a question - a lie marks the target\u2019s lips blood red.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* true red string - after tasting or otherwise ingesting a target\u2019s blood, can follow him at any distance.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* blood-splattered folding screens - adds (or increases) a bleed effect to a decisive attack.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* call to blood - mess with the target\u2019s blood pressure - can give an instant stroke to a trivial opponent. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* thicker than water - briefly create a dummy intimacy (positive or negative) in the target, towards a blood relative, providing leverage for social influence.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Essence 4</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* blood vow - make a promise binding by infusing the participants with the exalt\u2019s blood; it will become poison in their veins if the vow is broken.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* blood string marionette - cause bashing damage to the target - if it is enough to knock it out, control the liquids inside the body to move it like a puppet. </span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Essence 5</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* feed the dark mother - siphons blood from nearby corpses into the ground beneath the exalt\u2019s feet, gaining a temporary power boost.<br /> <br /> <b>For those I'm not only looking for ideas, but also for feedback regarding required essence levels - is there anything that should be moved up or down?</b></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T20:15:42-08:00","id":1351575,"title":"","content":"idea for path of blood essence one. Leave a trail of blood that does not vanish (maybe even can't cleaned) until next sunset (or midnight maybe). <br /> Can use to leave a trail in a labyrinth or as writing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}